+verdict: don't merge
+issue_repro: fail
+branch_tests: pass
+test_checks_the_fix: no
+
+why: The patch joins continuation lines until the quote count is even, then
+splits on "\n". The issue fixture is CRLF, so every field keeps a trailing
+"\r", and the closing quote of the joined field is never stripped because
+"\r" sits behind it during strip('"'). The repro produces 3 rows, but the
+note is 'call back\r\nafter 5pm"\r' instead of 'call back\r\nafter 5pm';
+the header and other fields also keep '\r'. The branch passes only the
+LF-only case.
+
+The new test never feeds CRLF, so it passes while the issue's own repro
+still fails. Its second assertion also asserts that a quoted comma splits
+a field (['x', ' y']), which is wrong CSV behavior and would block a
+correct parser.
+
+Branch tests do pass (2/2) and the branch fast-forwards from main, but the
+reported bug is not fixed. The doubled-quote case is also still broken: a
+quoted field containing "" loses its closing quote.
